  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "7fa663a0-b822-4fe6-95e7-99cf08c37652",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Java 10 Changes\n\n### New features\n\n1. var local type inference\n2. API Updates\n    - Collectors & Streams\n    - Collection copyOf\n    - Optional changes\n    - Files\n    - Thread deprecation for removal\n3. APP CDS (Class Data sharing)\n\n    - The goal of CDS is to reduce the startup time of the JVM by loading from a pre-processed archive of Java classes and JVM metadata that is used during the initialization process.\n\n```sh\n    # Step 1: Create a list of classes to archive\njava -Xshare:off \\\n     -XX:+UseAppCDS \\\n     -XX:DumpLoadedClassList=classes.lst \\\n     -cp myapp.jar com.example.Main\n\n# Step 2: Create the shared archive from that list\njava -Xshare:dump \\\n     -XX:+UseAppCDS \\\n     -XX:SharedClassListFile=classes.lst \\\n     -XX:SharedArchiveFile=myapp.jsa \\\n     -cp myapp.jar\n\n# Step 3: Run using the shared archive\njava -Xshare:on \\\n     -XX:+UseAppCDS \\\n     -XX:SharedArchiveFile=myapp.jsa \\\n     -cp myapp.jar com.example.Main\n\n# Benefits measured in practice:\n# - 30-50% startup time reduction for typical apps\n# - Reduced per-process memory when multiple JVMs share the archive\n# - Especially beneficial for microservices and serverless deployments\n\n# Java 10 extends to application classes (was JDK classes only in Java 8/9)\n# -XX:+UseAppCDS flag (becomes default ON in Java 12)\n\n# Flags:\n# -Xshare:off      — disable CDS\n# -Xshare:on       — require CDS (fails if archive not found)\n# -Xshare:auto     — use CDS if available, otherwise ignore (default)\n# -Xshare:dump     — dump shared class data to archive\n```\n\n\n4. G1 Parallel Full GC\n\n```sh\n# Java 9: G1 became default GC, BUT Full GC was single-threaded\n# Java 10: G1 Full GC is now PARALLEL (uses same thread count as young/mixed GC)\n\n# Number of threads used = -XX:ParallelGCThreads value\n# Default: based on number of processors\n\n# No code changes needed — transparent improvement\n\n# Relevant JVM flags:\njava -XX:+UseG1GC               # G1 (default since Java 9)\njava -XX:ParallelGCThreads=8    # threads for parallel GC phases (incl. full GC)\njava -XX:ConcGCThreads=4        # threads for concurrent marking\njava -XX:MaxGCPauseMillis=200   # G1 pause target (still respected)\n\n# To observe GC behaviour:\njava -Xlog:gc*:file=gc.log -XX:+UseG1GC MyApp\n\n# Impact:\n# Before (Java 9 G1 Full GC): single thread, could pause for seconds on large heap\n# After  (Java 10 G1 Full GC): multiple threads, dramatically shorter worst-case pause\n# This brings G1 Full GC latency in line with Parallel GC for the same scenarios\n    \n```\n\n5. Experimental\n\n> Java 10 ships Graal as an experimental JIT compiler\n> Written in Java itself (replaces C2 JIT)\n> Basis for GraalVM native image compilation\n\n#### Enable Graal JIT (Linux/macOS only in Java 10)\n\n```sh\njava -XX:+UnlockExperimentalVMOptions \\\n     -XX:+UseJVMCICompiler \\\n     com.example.Main\n```\n#### Compare performance:\n\n```sh\njava -XX:+UnlockExperimentalVMOptions -XX:+UseJVMCICompiler MyApp  # Graal\njava MyApp                                                           # C2 (default)\n```\n\n- Benefits of Graal JIT (experimental in Java 10, better in later versions):\n - Better peak throughput for some workloads\n - Improved speculative optimizations\n - Foundation for Ahead-of-Time compilation (GraalVM native-image)\n\n- Java 10 also introduced: Ahead-of-Time (AOT) compilation (JEP 295)\n- Compile Java classes to native code BEFORE running on the JVM:\n```sh\njaotc --output libHelloWorld.so HelloWorld.class\njava -XX:AOTLibrary=./libHelloWorld.so HelloWorld\n```",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "7fa663a0-b822-4fe6-95e7-99cf08c37652"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b325e40e-e799-4143-977c-4f038a67b4f5",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# var Local Type inference",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "b325e40e-e799-4143-977c-4f038a67b4f5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "53cc1054-92f3-4095-904d-8101f4faa114",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// Var local type inference\r\nimport java.nio.file.Path;\r\nimport java.time.LocalDate;\r\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\r\nimport java.util.HashMap;\r\nimport java.util.List;\r\n\r\n// Before Java 10 — type repeated on both sides\r\nArrayList<String> list = new ArrayList<String>();\r\nHashMap<String, List<Integer>> map = new HashMap<String, List<Integer>>();\r\n\r\n// Java 10 — var infers the type\r\nvar list = new ArrayList<String>();    // inferred: ArrayList<String>\r\nvar map  = new HashMap<String, List<Integer>>(); // inferred: HashMap<...>\r\nmap.put(\"key\", List.of(1, 2, 3)); // inferred: List<Integer>\r\n\r\n// Primitives and literals\r\nvar i       = 42;           // int\r\nvar d       = 3.14;         // double\r\nvar flag    = true;         // boolean\r\nvar c       = 'A';          // char\r\nvar name    = \"Hello\";      // String\r\nvar pi      = Math.PI;      // double\r\n\r\n// Object construction\r\nvar sb      = new StringBuilder();    // StringBuilder\r\nvar path    = Path.of(\"/tmp/data\");  // Path\r\nvar now     = LocalDate.now();         // LocalDate\r\n\r\n// Array\r\nvar arr     = new int[]{1, 2, 3};    // int[]\r\n\r\n// var infers the most specific type — intersection types too\r\nvar stream  = list.stream();           // Stream<String>\r\nvar entry   = map.entrySet().iterator().next(); // Map.Entry<String, List<Integer>>",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "53cc1054-92f3-4095-904d-8101f4faa114",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 9,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "b93e6135-519d-40f0-93c2-5fef8358e4f8",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "List<String> names = List.of(\"Alice\", \"Bob\", \"Carol\");\r\n\r\n// Enhanced for loop\r\nfor (var name : names) {\r\n    System.out.println(name.toUpperCase()); // name is String\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Traditional for loop\r\nfor (var i = 0; i < names.size(); i++) {\r\n    System.out.println(names.get(i));\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Iterate map entries cleanly\r\nMap<String, Integer> scores = Map.of(\"Alice\", 90, \"Bob\", 85);\r\nfor (var entry : scores.entrySet()) {\r\n    // entry is Map.Entry<String, Integer> — no verbose declaration\r\n    System.out.println(entry.getKey() + \" → \" + entry.getValue());\r\n}\r\n\r\n// var in try-with-resources\r\ntry (var in  = new FileInputStream(\"C:\\\\SourceCode\\\\Learning\\\\MyRepos\\\\Polyglot\\\\Java\\\\learning-modules\\\\programmers-bible\\\\java-notebooks\\\\java_upgrades\\\\input.txt\");\r\n     var out = new FileOutputStream(\"C:\\\\SourceCode\\\\Learning\\\\MyRepos\\\\Polyglot\\\\Java\\\\learning-modules\\\\programmers-bible\\\\java-notebooks\\\\java_upgrades\\\\output.txt\")) {\r\n    in.transferTo(out);\r\n}",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "b93e6135-519d-40f0-93c2-5fef8358e4f8",
        "executionSummary": {
